/*
# Dialog

The modal tier (planes.md): a full-app SCRIM that swallows every press —
modal input blocking, no light dismiss — under a centered panel with a
focusTrap. Buttons are RECORDS (the records door): `{ id, label,
default?, cancel? }`, rendered as themed library Buttons right-aligned in
the platform arrangement. Focus SAVES on open and RETURNS on close.

Keyboard: Return picks the DEFAULT button (the macOS rule; a focused
button also activates on Space/Enter — the pick guard makes the double
harmless), Escape picks the cancel record when one exists, else just
closes.

The idioms — one verb each, an optional callback receiving the picked id
(the `picked(id)` override remains the declarative seam):

    dlg.notice("Saved", "Your changes were saved.")
    dlg.ask("Save changes?", "Unsaved changes will be lost.", (id) => …)
    dlg.error("Could not connect", "The server refused the connection.")

`ask` is Cancel / No / Yes-default; `error` renders the title in the
theme's errorColor.

Platform STRUCTURE is data (the scheme): `dialogWidth`,
`dialogButtons` = "end" (a right-aligned row — SF, Material) | "stack"
(the macOS alert — full-width buttons stacked, DEFAULT ON TOP) | "fill"
(WinUI ContentDialog — equal-width buttons filling the row),
`dialogAlign` = "left" | "center" (the macOS centered title),
`dialogTitleSize` / `dialogBodySize`. Plus scrimColor + scrimOpacity
(macOS barely dims — alerts separate by SHADOW; Material's spec scrim is
32%; Fluent's smoke 30%), the menuShadow family, errorColor.

**Declare one and call it.** A `Dialog` is not a view you show and hide around your
content — it is a standing member you open with a verb, so the same instance serves
every prompt in the program.

```declare
App [ width = 340, height = 140, said: string = "",
    dlg: Dialog [ ],
    Button [ x = 20, y = 20, label = "Delete…",
        onClick() { app.dlg.ask("Delete this file?", "This cannot be undone.",
                                (id) => { app.said = id }) }
        ],
    Text [ x = 20, y = 80, text = { app.said == "" ? "—" : "you chose: " + app.said } ]
    ]
```

## shown
Whether the dialog is up. Read it; **open through a verb** (`ask`, `notice`, `error`,
`open`) rather than assigning it, or you get a panel with no buttons, no saved focus,
and no focus trap engaged.

## picked()
**The declarative delivery seam — override it at the use site.** Receives the picked
button's `id`. Fires after the dialog has left the screen, and *in addition to* any
callback passed to the verb, so you may use either or both.

## ask()
The three-way prompt: Cancel / No / Yes, with Yes as the default. Delivers `"cancel"`,
`"no"` or `"yes"`.

## notice()
A single-OK acknowledgement. Delivers `"ok"`.

## error()
A single-OK acknowledgement with the title in the theme's error colour. Delivers `"ok"`.

## open()
The general form the three idioms are built on: title, message, your own button
records, a tone (`"error"` or `""`), and an optional callback. Reach for it when the
three idioms do not spell your choices — **button records are `{ id, label, default?,
cancel? }`**, and the two flags are what Return and Escape key off.

## close()
Takes the dialog down without delivering anything, and restores focus to whatever held
it before. **Focus is restored one turn later, deliberately** — an immediate restore
hands the in-flight keystroke back to the opener, which re-activates and reopens.

## pick()
Delivers a button by id: **dismisses first, then delivers**, one painted frame later —
the same contract as `Menu.pick`, so a slow action cannot freeze the dialog on screen.
Guarded against double activation, so a focused default button answering Space *and*
Return is harmless.

## pickDefault()
Picks whichever button record carries `default: true` — Return's action, the macOS rule.

## pickCancel()
Picks the `cancel: true` record when there is one, else just closes — Escape's action.
**A dialog with no cancel record still dismisses on Escape**, it simply delivers
nothing.

## title
The heading. Set by the verbs; read it if you are restyling.

## message
The body text under the title. `""` hides the line entirely rather than leaving a gap.

## buttons
The button records currently rendered, in authored order. The `"stack"` arrangement
reorders them for display — default on top, cancel at the bottom — without touching
this.

## tone
`"error"` tints the title with the theme's error colour; `""` is the ordinary tone.

## arrangement
How the buttons lay out, elected by `theme.dialogButtons`: `"end"` (a right-aligned
row), `"stack"` (full-width buttons stacked, macOS-style, default on top), or `"fill"`
(equal-width buttons filling the row). **Platform structure is data, not a fork.**

## centered
Whether the title and message are centre-aligned, elected by `theme.dialogAlign`.

## focusDefault()
Puts keyboard focus on the default button when the dialog opens — or the last button
when no record is marked default.

## saved
**Internal.** The view that held focus when the dialog opened, restored on close.

## cb
**Internal.** The callback handed to the opening verb.

## callCb()
**Internal.** Invokes the stored callback.

## kidsOf()
**Internal.** The rendered button views of an arrangement, for `focusDefault`.
*/

include [ "control.declare" ]

include [ "button.declare" ]

class Dialog extends View [ visible = { shown },
    x = 0,
    y = 0,
    width = { app.width },
    height = { app.height },

    shown: boolean = false,
    title: string = "",
    message: string = "",
    tone: string = "",
    buttons: array = null,
    saved: View = null,
    cb: (id: string) -> void? = null,

    // the delivery seam — override declaratively, or pass a callback to a verb

    picked(id: string) { },

    open(t: string, m: string, btns: array, tone_: string, cb_: (id: string) -> void?) {
        title = "" + (t || "")
        message = "" + (m || "")
        tone = "" + (tone_ || "")
        buttons = btns
        this.cb = cb_ || null
        saved = Focus.getFocus()
        shown = true
        this.raise()
        setTimeout(() => this.focusDefault(), 0)
        },

    // ── the idioms ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    notice(t: string, m: string, cb_: (id: string) -> void?) { this.open(t, m, [({ id: "ok", label: "OK", default: true })], "", cb_) },

    error(t: string, m: string, cb_: (id: string) -> void?) { this.open(t, m, [({ id: "ok", label: "OK", default: true })], "error", cb_) },

    ask(t: string, m: string, cb_: (id: string) -> void?) {
        this.open(t, m, [
            ({ id: "cancel", label: "Cancel", cancel: true }),
            ({ id: "no", label: "No" }),
            ({ id: "yes", label: "Yes", default: true }),
        ], "", cb_)
        },

    close() {
        shown = false
        const s = saved
        saved = null
        // restore DEFERRED: the in-flight keystroke must finish against the
        // OLD focus — an immediate restore hands the same Enter to the opener,
        // which re-activates and reopens (the re-entry the probe caught)
        if (s != null) setTimeout(() => Focus.focus(s), 0)
        },

    // Dismiss-then-deliver, the same contract as Menu's pick: transient
    // chrome leaves the screen (one painted frame) before the action runs,
    // so a slow verb can never freeze the dialog in place.

    pick(id: string) {
        if (!shown) return                       // the double-activation guard
        const f = this.cb
        this.close()
        const deliver = () => { this.picked(id); if (f != null) this.callCb(f, id) }
        const raf = (globalThis as any).requestAnimationFrame
        if (typeof raf == "function") raf(() => setTimeout(deliver, 0))
        else setTimeout(deliver, 0)
        },

    callCb(f: (id: string) -> void, id: string) { f(id) },

    kidsOf(b: View) -> array { return b.children },

    focusDefault() {
        if (!shown) return
        const b = this.panel.col.btns
        const kids = this.kidsOf(this.arrangement == "stack" ? b.stackInner : b.rowInner)
        const d = kids.find((k) => k.primary)
        Focus.focus(d != null ? d : kids.length > 0 ? kids[kids.length - 1] : null)
        },

    pickDefault() {
        const b = (this.buttons || []).find((x) => x.default)
        if (b != null) this.pick("" + b.id)
        },

    pickCancel() {
        const b = (this.buttons || []).find((x) => x.cancel)
        if (b != null) this.pick("" + b.id)
        else this.close()
        },

    keys: Keys [
        onKeyDown(e: KeyEvent) {
            if (!classroot.shown) return
            if (e.key == "Enter") classroot.pickDefault()
            else if (e.key == "Escape") classroot.pickCancel()
            }
        ],

    // buttons → Button instances through the internal derived dataset. The
    // "stack" arrangement REORDERS: the default on top, cancel at the bottom
    // (the macOS stacked alert); row arrangements keep authored order.

    arrangement: string = { typeof theme.dialogButtons == "string" ? theme.dialogButtons : "end" },
    centered: boolean = { theme.dialogAlign == "center" },

    data: Dataset [ contents = { ({ b: classroot.arrangement == "stack"
        ? [...(classroot.buttons || [])].sort((p, q) => (q.default ? 1 : q.cancel ? -1 : 0) - (p.default ? 1 : p.cancel ? -1 : 0))
        : classroot.buttons || [] }) } ],

    // the scrim: MODAL input blocking — every press lands here and stops

    scrim: View [ x = 0, y = 0, width = { app.width }, height = { app.height },
        fill = { theme.scrimColor != null ? theme.scrimColor : 0x000000 },
        opacity = { typeof theme.scrimOpacity == "number" ? theme.scrimOpacity : 0.32 },
        onPointerDown() { }
        ],

    panel: View [ focusTrap = true,
        width = { typeof theme.dialogWidth == "number" ? theme.dialogWidth : 420 },
        x = { (app.width - this.width) / 2 },
        y = { Math.max(40, (app.height - this.height) / 3) },
        height = { this.col.height + 40 },
        cornerRadius = { typeof theme.menuRadius == "number" ? theme.menuRadius + 2 : 10 },
        fill = { theme.surface },
        stroke = { stroke(1, theme.line) },
        shadow = { theme.menuShadow != null ? theme.menuShadow : shadow(0, 12, 48, 0x00000040) },

        col: View [ x = 20, y = 20, width = { parent.width - 40 },
            layout: SimpleLayout [ axis = y, spacing = 12 ],

            ttl: Text [ fontWeight = bold, wrap = true, width = { parent.width },
                fontSize = { typeof theme.dialogTitleSize == "number" ? theme.dialogTitleSize : 15 },
                textAlign = { classroot.centered ? "center" : "left" },
                textColor = { classroot.tone == "error" ? (theme.errorColor != null ? theme.errorColor : 0xC93429) : theme.text },
                text = { classroot.title } ],

            msg: Text [ wrap = true, width = { parent.width },
                fontSize = { typeof theme.dialogBodySize == "number" ? theme.dialogBodySize : 13 },
                textAlign = { classroot.centered ? "center" : "left" },
                visible = { classroot.message != "" },
                textColor = { theme.textMuted }, text = { classroot.message } ],

            gap: View [ width = 4, height = 4 ],

            btns: View [ width = { parent.width },
                height = { classroot.arrangement == "stack" ? this.stackInner.height : this.rowInner.height },

                // two arrangements, one visible — layout attributes are
                // literal-only (the surface), so the axes are two containers

                rowInner: View [ visible = { classroot.arrangement != "stack" },
                    height = { this.contentHeight },
                    x = { classroot.arrangement == "end" ? parent.width - this.width : 0 },
                    width = { classroot.arrangement == "end" ? this.contentWidth : parent.width },
                    layout: SimpleLayout [ axis = x, spacing = 10 ],
                    datapath = { classroot.data.value },
                    Button [ datapath = :b[], label = { "" + :label },
                        width = { classroot.arrangement == "fill"
                                ? (this.parent.width - 10 * (((classroot.buttons || []).length || 1) - 1)) / ((classroot.buttons || []).length || 1)
                                : 86 },
                        primary = { !!:default },
                        onClick() { classroot.pick("" + :id) }
                        ]
                    ],

                stackInner: View [ visible = { classroot.arrangement == "stack" },
                    height = { this.contentHeight }, width = { parent.width },
                    layout: SimpleLayout [ axis = y, spacing = 8 ],
                    datapath = { classroot.data.value },
                    Button [ datapath = :b[], label = { "" + :label },
                        width = { this.parent.width },
                        primary = { !!:default },
                        onClick() { classroot.pick("" + :id) }
                        ]
                    ]
                ]
            ]
        ]
    ]
